@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Tooltip}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Accessibility}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tooltip @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Tooltip @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Accessibility</h1>

<p>
    The tooltip's behaviour is governed primarily by <abbr title="Web Content Accessibility Guidelines">WCAG</abbr>
    <strong>1.4.13 Content on Hover or Focus</strong> (Level AA), which applies to any additional content such as a tooltip that appears on hover or keyboard focus and
    disappears when the user moves away. This criterion has three requirements, each reflected in how this component is built:
</p>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Dismissible</strong> — the tooltip can be closed without moving the pointer or keyboard focus, typically with the <kbd class="@CodeSpan.Base">Escape</kbd> key, and doing so does not
    unintentionally close anything else on the page.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Hoverable</strong> — the pointer can move from the trigger onto the tooltip content itself without the tooltip disappearing.
  </li>
  <li>
    <strong>Persistent</strong> — the tooltip remains visible until the user dismisses it, moves focus or the pointer away, or its content is no longer valid; it does not
    time out on its own.
  </li>
</ul>
<p>
    Two further criteria also apply: <strong>4.1.2 Name, Role, Value</strong> (Level A), satisfied via <code class="@CodeSpan.Base">role="tooltip"</code> and the <code>aria-describedby</code>
    relationship you provide on the trigger element, and <strong>2.1.1 Keyboard</strong> (Level A), satisfied by the tooltip appearing on keyboard focus as well as on hover.
</p>

<h2 id="tooltip-keyboard">Keyboard interaction</h2>
<ul aria-labelledby="tooltip-keyboard">
    <li><kbd class="@Kbd.Base @Kbd.Scheme(KbdScheme.Neutral)">Tab</kbd> - moves focus to the focusable item that the tooltip is wrapping.</li>
    <li><kbd class="@Kbd.Base @Kbd.Scheme(KbdScheme.Neutral)">Escape</kbd> - closes the tooltip.</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Note:</strong> to assist pointer users where it may be difficult to use the escape key, an un-focusable but clickable close icon is also available.
</p>


<h2 id="device-testing">Accessibility device testing</h2>

<ul aria-labelledby="device-testing">
    <li>JAWS, Narrator and NVDA on Windows were each paired with every one of the following browsers: Google Chrome, Microsoft Edge and Mozilla Firefox.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on macOS was paired with Apple's Safari.</li>
    <li>VoiceOver on iPhone was paired with mobile Safari.</li>
    <li>Talkback on Android was paired with mobile Google Chrome.</li>
    <li>Voice access on Windows 11</li>
</ul>

<p>
    <strong>Note: </strong> Testing was performed with the latest browser and assistive technologies versions that were available at the time of testing (see release history on the installation page for approximate testing dates)
</p>

